provides an interface for displaying the OpenPROM or OpenFirmware
device  tree  and node properties.  The program is only installed
on supported platforms.  Without any  arguments,  will  dump  the
full  tree.  When given the name of a specific node, will display
that node and its child nodes.  The options are  as  follows:  On
systems with OpenPROM, use instead of the default On systems with
OpenFirmware,  use  instead  of  the  default Dump a partial tree
starting from Display each node’s properties.  Instead of reading
from the openprom or openfirm device, use the proplib file as in‐
put.  See also Display the full path name for each  node.   Write
the  device tree to the proplib file See also The openprom device
on systems with OpenPROM.  The openfirm device  on  systems  with
OpenFirmware.
